@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@
 M17..M19 are done in this base (M21 part 1: power, wire, torch, lever, button, plates) (soul sand waits for M11). Next in the easy-first order: the rest of M20 (compass and clock, taming, saddle), then M22, M11, M14; M21 (redstone) is the biggest and gets a session of its own. First run `cargo test --lib`: the M15..M19 work has never been compiled.
 
 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-14: Console-Edition look, the rest (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +5 tests `sky::tests::{fan_hugs_the_sun_at_the_horizon, celestial_texture_is_sun_and_moon}` (+ the sky shader test now lists `vs_stars`, `vs_fan`, `vs_body`, `fs_body`, `fs_geo`), `hud::tests::{gui_sheet_has_the_sprites, containers_sheet_has_the_panels, cube_icon_fits_its_box, button_is_ends_and_middle}`, `atlas::tests::every_handed_out_tile_has_a_picture`; none run). Merged from twelve earlier patches, on top of the legacy frame that was already in:
+    - Sky: the sunrise / sunset fan (`sky::fan_vertices`, 16 triangles from `sunrise_color`), the stars (`star_vertices`, brightness x (1 - rain)) and the sun and moon (quads of 60 and 40 at distance 100, `assets/celestial.rgba` from the Legacy Restoration pack, additive like the Java) are geometry drawn by `SkyRenderer::draw_extras` right after `draw`, in the same pass, depth `LessEqual`, no depth write. Under water the legacy fog is b1.7.3's GL_EXP (density 0.1, colour 0.02 / 0.02 / 0.2; a negative `far` carries the density to `apply_fog`). Water is flat in legacy: no depth absorption, no grazing reflection (`fs_water`).
+    - Blocks: `tools/gen_terrain_pack.py` rewrites `assets/terrain.rgba` from the pack, slot by slot (149 slots; UNTINTED, like `gen_terrain.py`: the mesher tints; leaves opaque, lava / ice opaque, water alpha 138; chests, the beds and the slots the pack has nothing for keep the png's tile). `terrain_tile` gets the dispenser, note block, cobweb, portal and locked chest.
+    - HUD: the HUD texture is 256 x 2048 (items, `assets/gui.rgba` = widgets.png over icons.png, terrain.png, `assets/containers.rgba` = the four container panels; `tools/gen_gui.py`). Hotbar strip + selector, hearts, the armor bar, air bubbles and the crosshair are its sprites (`hud::sprites`, `HudPipeline::push_gui`); block stacks are isometric cubes (`push_cube`, top / left / right lit 1.0 / 0.8 / 0.6, a slab half high, grass and leaves tinted for the plains) or their flat tile (`push_block_icon`); the inventory, workbench, furnace and chest screens are the pack's panels (furnace arrow and flame are its sprites) with the `GuiContainer` labels; the pause and inventory buttons and the pause menu use `widgets.png` buttons (`push_button`) with centred labels.
+    - UNVERIFIED: which sides of a block icon face the viewer; the furnace / crafting label positions (recalled); the 4-pixel ends of the touch buttons stretched to ~120 px; the black player-model box in the inventory (as in the pack). Not done: the player model, a dispenser panel (no dispenser logic), the tooltip box texture.
 - 2026-10-14: M21 part 1, redstone power (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +2 tests, extended `pick` test). `world/redstone.rs` is the read side, a literal port of `World.isBlockProvidingPowerTo` / `isBlockGettingPowered` / `isBlockIndirectlyProvidingPowerTo` / `isBlockIndirectlyGettingPowered` with the weak / strong `isPoweringTo` of each block (`wires` = `wiresProvidePower`); `ticks.rs` is the write side. Wire: `BlockRedstoneWire`'s recursive propagation is one local recomputation (`wire_level`: 15 when anything but a wire powers it, else the strongest neighbouring wire - 1, also one step up / down) applied by `neighbour`; a change is written with `set_block_meta`, whose log entry makes the next wires recompute (max-minus-one converges, a loop of dust decays to 0), and `wire_ends` pings the four side cells so wires one step up or down hear of it (`notifyWireNeighborsOfNeighborChange`). `ChunkManager::ping` = `notifyBlocksOfNeighborChange` (a log entry with sentinel id 255); `neighbour` now gets the id that changed (`onNeighborBlockChange`'s last argument; 255 counts as a power source) and `notify` pings the neighbours of a lever / button / plate / torch that changed (the block it points at hears too). Torch 75 / 76: `torch` = `updateTick` (input from the block it hangs on, 2-tick delay, 8 flips in 100 ticks burn it out; no fizz, no smoke). Lever / button: right click (`App::use_block`), button released by a 20-tick scheduled update. Plates: `Ticks::plates` (every tick, boxes of the player and the mobs in `plate_ents`) = `onEntityCollidedWithBlock`, `plate` = `setStateIfMobInteractsWithPlate` re-checked every 20 ticks; stone wants a living thing, wood anything (ponytail: items and arrows do not press it). Glowing ore 74: lit by a right click or by walking on it (`Ticks::walk`), reverts on a random tick. Doors / trapdoors open while powered (`onPoweredBlockChange`), TNT is lit by power (M18 follow-up). Rendering: dust is one flat quad (tile 164) tinted by level (`colorMultiplier`), levers / buttons / plates are boxes (`box_bounds`), redstone torches share `push_torch` (tiles 99 / 115). ponytail: the lever is its sprite on a box (no base and handle), a punch does not flip a lever or light an ore, dust always uses the cross tile, no click sounds, no reddust particles.
 - 2026-10-14: M19 sign + painting, M17 cactus on mobs, M18 TNT recipe + flash (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +5 tests `decor::tests::{paintings_hang_on_walls_like_java, paintings_fall_off_and_are_picked, signs_place_edit_and_save}`, `mobs::tests::cactus_hurts_a_mob_without_knockback_or_anger`, asserts in `plain_recipes_match_java` and `atlas`). Ported from `EntityPainting`, `EnumArt`, `ItemPainting`, `RenderPainting`, `BlockSign`, `ItemSign`, `TileEntitySign`, `TileEntitySignRenderer`, `SignModel`, `GuiEditSign`, `BlockCactus`, `RenderTNTPrimed`:
     - `world/decor.rs` (new): `ART` (`EnumArt`), `Painting` (`func_412_b` frame, `func_410_i` = `fits`: no collision box in the plate, solid wall behind each 16 px piece, no other painting; `hang` draws one of the motives that fit with `nextInt`; `step` re-checks every 101 ticks and the caller drops the item; `pick` = ray against the box grown 0.1), `sign_place` (`ItemSign.onItemUse`: post `floor((rotationYaw + 180) * 16 / 360 + 0.5) & 15` on a top face, wall sign with the face as metadata), the editor (`Edit`, `Key`, `layout`: an on-screen keyboard, `GuiEditSign.keyTyped` = 15 characters, backspace, next line) and the `decor` save file (own file: `Level`'s optional tails stay as they are; a line or motive out of range makes the file be ignored).
